<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iron Age</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">from c. 1200 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Iron Age is the period in which iron replaced bronze as the main metal for tools and weapons, beginning in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">Near East</a> around 1200 BCE and reaching northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> several centuries later. Its dates differ by region. In the histories of Levantine cities, Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polis">poleis</a>, Iberian and British peoples and Scandinavian districts it marks the age of hillforts, new kingdoms and the first written records.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iron-age.jpg" alt="Iron Age" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HMB_Keltengrab_M%C3%BCnsingen-Rain_Grab_91.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
